### Lab 1 – REST examples (VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ HTTP client)
@app = http://localhost:8081

### 1. Start a loan application (creates a process instance)
POST {{app}}/api/loan-applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "LA-TC01",
  "applicantId": "SYN-APP-1001",
  "applicantName": "Asha Synthetic",
  "age": 34,
  "email": "applicant@example.com",
  "loanAmount": 20000,
  "loanTermMonths": 48,
  "monthlyIncome": 6500,
  "monthlyDebt": 400,
  "employmentStatus": "EMPLOYED",
  "loanPurpose": "HOME_IMPROVEMENT"
}

# Response 201:
# {"processInstanceKey": 2251799813685649, "processDefinitionVersion": 1, "applicationId": "LA-TC01"}

### 2. Mock credit-assessment API – the call the REST Connector makes
POST {{app}}/api/credit/assessments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: LA-TC01

{
  "applicationId": "LA-TC01",
  "applicantId": "SYN-APP-1001",
  "applicantName": "Asha Synthetic",
  "loanAmount": 20000,
  "monthlyIncome": 6500,
  "monthlyDebt": 400
}

# Response 200:
# {"assessmentId":"CA-75F0E0B3","applicantId":"SYN-APP-1001","creditScore":782,"riskBand":"LOW",
#  "existingDefaults":0,"assessedAt":"2026-10-28T08:28:37.051627700+05:30"}

### 3. Simulated API error (any applicantId starting with SYN-ERR)
POST {{app}}/api/credit/assessments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicantId": "SYN-ERR-0001" }

# Response 503:
# {"error":"CREDIT_BUREAU_UNAVAILABLE","message":"Simulated credit bureau outage"}

### 4. Switch the whole mock API into failure mode (ERROR | TIMEOUT | NORMAL)
PUT {{app}}/api/mock/credit/mode/ERROR

### 5. Back to normal
PUT {{app}}/api/mock/credit/mode/NORMAL
